  <prompt>Make the critical Cosmos transcript write awaited/confirmed for messages[0] (the first turn) so the transcript + title seed survive Redis eviction; keep remaining turns async; spec a latency budget.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. .NET 8 Minimal API + AI session-persistence expertise; comfortable splitting a fire-and-forget write into a confirmed first-turn write within the ADR-040 3-tier cascade.</role>
  <goal>After a session's first turn, the Cosmos StoredSession contains messages[0] before the request completes; reopening after Redis TTL shows the transcript, not a blank pane.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-D2 — the Cosmos transcript write is fire-and-forget today (ChatSessionManager.FireAndForgetCosmosPersist:574-587 / SessionPersistenceService.UpsertToCosmosAsync:863-879), so a session's first turn can be lost to Redis eviction, leaving a blank pane on reopen. Owner Option A: make only the FIRST turn's write awaited/confirmed; keep later turns async.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ChatSessionManager.cs (FireAndForgetCosmosPersist:574-587, UpdateSessionCacheAsync:298-306)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Sessions/SessionPersistenceService.cs (PersistSessionAsync:211-220, UpsertToCosmosAsync:863-879)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">Stay within the existing 3-tier cascade — no new store; only the FIRST turn's write becomes awaited.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">NFR-03 — the awaited write adds bounded latency to the first turn only; record a latency budget.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Publish size ≤60 MB — report the delta (BFF §10).</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
