    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Identify the first-turn path (messages[0]) vs subsequent turns.</step>
    <step order="2">Await/confirm the Cosmos upsert for messages[0]; leave later turns fire-and-forget.</step>
    <step order="3">Add a unit test asserting messages[0] is in Cosmos before the request completes.</step>
    <step order="4">dotnet build + publish size check.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If awaiting messages[0] pushes first-turn latency beyond a reasonable budget, STOP and escalate with the measured numbers rather than awaiting all turns.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>FireAndForgetCosmosPersist:583 deliberately does not await; no reliable first-turn write.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — split the first-turn write out of the fire-and-forget path.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A session's first turn can be lost to Redis eviction → blank pane on reopen.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ChatSessionManager.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Sessions/SessionPersistenceService.cs</output>
